## Where to find it

**Analytics** in the side drawer. It isn't a single dashboard — it's six pages, each grouped around
one kind of decision rather than around one screen of the app:

| Page | What it's for |
| --- | --- |
| **Overview** | The starting point — the headline picture across the institute. |
| **Students & Risk** | Which individual students need attention. |
| **Academics** | Exam and assessment performance. |
| **Attendance** | Attendance together with punctuality. |
| **Payments** | Fees charged against fees actually collected. |
| **Operations** | How the institute is running day to day. |

**Payments** and **Operations** are admin-only. If you're a teacher or coordinator, those two won't
appear in your Analytics group — that's the intended access split, not a missing page.

## Narrowing to one class

Most pages accept a class filter, and the class you pick is carried in the page's own address. That
means a filtered view can be bookmarked or pasted to a colleague and it will open on the same class
for them — provided they have access to that page in the first place.

## Old links still work

The analytics section was reorganised from a single six-tab dashboard into these separate pages.
Older bookmarks and saved links still resolve:

- Numbered tab links (the original `?tab=` style) land on the matching page.
- The retired page names redirect to their new homes — *Exams* → **Academics**, *Financial* →
  **Payments**, *Punctuality* → **Attendance** (punctuality was merged in), and *Intelligence* →
  **Students & Risk**.

In every case the class you had selected is carried across, so you don't lose your filter. There's
no need to hunt down and update old links.

